    "$comment": "D244 R-14 (owner: \"cannabis is dried and then cured. it is called the cure process... so it cant block us... looking at the words before and after\"). A BLOCK-pattern hit on a single word listed in a family below is judged by the words around it. Medical window: the sentence, `window.before` words before and `window.after` words after; any medicalWords there keeps the block (except a medical word right after medicalNeutralBefore, e.g. 'low stress', or right before medicalNeutralAfter, e.g. 'disease-free'). Reach checks look only inside the same clause (commas split clauses). default 'allow' (the cure family): warn-only unless a medicalBefore/medicalAfter word is within reach, medicalAfterAtEnd ends the clause ('a cure-all'), or 'for' follows without a time ('cured for 21 days' ok, 'a cure for a bad day' blocks). default 'block': still blocks unless a benignBefore/benignAfter word is within reach. An allowed hit becomes a heads-up flag, never silent. Consumed by src/lib/ai/compliance-context-core.ts and crawler/app/compliance.py (same algorithm); `examples` are run by BOTH sides' tests.",
